# The Arcade module's MAME: Debian's (GPL-2.0+), the emulator and its data,
# among which its plugins (the hiscore plugin, with hiscore.dat, which keeps
# the games' high scores). About 450 MB with what it depends on. And its second
# engine, for RetroAchievements' high scores and online play: Debian's
# RetroArch (GPL-3.0), which brings the assets its menu reads (what it knows of
# the core OSD/OS writes for each game) and the libraries RetroArch needs;
# FinalBurn Neo, the core it plays the games with, comes with the app, and so
# does the RetroArch they play in, the same version built with TLS
# (scripts/build-retroarch.sh). 00-run.sh checks both versions against
# scripts/engines.env.
# os/build.sh skips it all with OSDOS_ARCADE=0; the module then says MAME is
# not installed.
mame mame-data retroarch
